# Rule Induction with Extension Matrices.

**Authors:** Wu, Xindong

## Abstract
Presents a heuristic, attribute-based, noise-tolerant data mining program, HCV (Version 2.0) based on the newly-developed extension matrix approach. Outlines some techniques implemented in the HCV program for noise handling and discretization of continuous domains; an empirical comparison shows that rules generated by HCV are more compact than the decision trees or rules produced by ID3-like data mining algorithms. (AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ564268

